  "implementation_rules": [
    "Use these values as absolute anchors for a TWO-LINE-ITEM invoice. The approved PDF has 2 lines; do not confuse baseline_top_pt with glyph bounds.",
    "For each additional item, increase line-item space by row_height_pt (47.0) and push downstream blocks down or page-break cleanly; never blindly overlap footer. For fewer items, maintain sensible whitespace.",
    "Use text metrics to wrap long descriptions within the description column while avoiding collision with numerical columns. Grow affected rows and reflow following content.",
    "For dynamic amount strings and customer names, use measured text widths and right alignment, and never shrink everything to fit a single page.",
    "At the bottom of page 1 with 2 rows, payment panel is 578.89..716.89; payment terms end about y=757; footer rule is y=777.89. With an additional 47pt row, there is no room for all these blocks; continue on the next page rather than overlapping.",
    "The approved design uses Lato, not Helvetica. Locate or register Lato font files locally (including Semibold and Black weights). Do not share font files in deliverables.",
    "Fit a supplied logo inside the given 61.6x52.096pt box without stretching it.",
    "Refinement A uses 0.5pt PDF word spacing for natural multi-word content. Include word spacing in wrapping and right-aligned width calculations; do not apply it to letter-spaced labels, identifiers, email addresses, account numbers, or monetary values.",
    "Use the supplied business.json and invoice.json values rather than embedding personal/contact/banking details in code or this numeric spec.",
    "Prototype-only text DESIGN PREVIEW / NOT ISSUED should not appear on production output.",
    "Do not print TAX INVOICE, VAT or business address in current preview, but do not represent the template as SARS-compliant for taxable sales.",
    "If a strict two-row design cannot fit long descriptions with exact anchors, retain typography, columns and margins, then grow rows and paginate. Accessibility/readability trumps false pixel-perfect matches."
  ]
